WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.982
The next morning, the Barth children were feeling much better.

2
00:00:03.983 --> 00:00:06.760
Still, they missed their parents very much.

3
00:00:06.761 --> 00:00:10.533
It was over a week since Mom and Dad had left.

4
00:00:10.534 --> 00:00:12.812
Of course they called every night.

5
00:00:12.813 --> 00:00:17.497
But it wasn't the same.

6
00:00:17.498 --> 00:00:21.702
"I hope Mom and Dad come home soon," said Bobby.

7
00:00:21.703 --> 00:00:26.832
"I miss them so much," Jane said, almost in tears.

8
00:00:26.833 --> 00:00:30.831
"Dad has to find a job first," said Cy bravely.

9
00:00:30.832 --> 00:00:34.285
Inside, he, too, missed his parents.

10
00:00:34.286 --> 00:00:38.379
"I wish he would find one today," said Panther.

11
00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:41.767
Almost at the same time, the children looked up.

12
00:00:41.768 --> 00:00:45.243
"Are you thinking what I'm thinking?" asked Cy.

13
00:00:45.244 --> 00:00:48.907
"Huey," Bobby said under his breath.

14
00:00:48.908 --> 00:00:52.681
"But we said no more wishes," argued Panther.

15
00:00:52.682 --> 00:00:56.036
"Each of us got two wishes. That's it!"

16
00:00:56.037 --> 00:00:58.530
"But this is different," said Cy.

17
00:00:58.531 --> 00:01:01.639
"It's not for us, it's for Mom and Dad."

18
00:01:01.640 --> 00:01:04.494
The children thought about this.

19
00:01:04.495 --> 00:01:08.458
"And we didn't say good-bye to Huey," added Jane.

20
00:01:08.459 --> 00:01:11.616
"That's true," admitted Panther.

21
00:01:11.617 --> 00:01:15.418
So the children set out to see Huey once again.

22
00:01:15.419 --> 00:01:17.834
Cy lowered the bucket as usual.

23
00:01:17.835 --> 00:01:21.078
But it took longer to locate Huey's shell.

24
00:01:21.079 --> 00:01:24.268
Finally Cy found him and pulled him up.

25
00:01:24.269 --> 00:01:26.285
"Where were you, Huey?"

26
00:01:26.286 --> 00:01:29.493
asked Cy when the magical creature appeared.

27
00:01:29.494 --> 00:01:31.807
"Just busy with something,"

28
00:01:31.808 --> 00:01:34.594
Huey answered, avoiding their eyes.

29
00:01:34.596 --> 00:01:37.686
Huey seemed different from his usual self.

30
00:01:37.687 --> 00:01:41.536
But the children were afraid to ask if something had happened to him.

31
00:01:41.537 --> 00:01:43.715
"Whose turn is it today?"

32
00:01:43.716 --> 00:01:46.774
Huey said, his voice back to normal.

33
00:01:46.775 --> 00:01:48.950
The children looked at each other.

34
00:01:48.951 --> 00:01:53.381
Then Cy answered, "Well, it's our wish."

35
00:01:53.382 --> 00:01:56.232
He pointed to his siblings and himself.

36
00:01:56.233 --> 00:01:58.636
Huey looked surprised.

37
00:01:58.637 --> 00:02:03.721
"That's unusual. What is your wish, then?"

38
00:02:03.722 --> 00:02:08.284
"We wish our dad would find a job," said Cy.

39
00:02:08.285 --> 00:02:12.219
"And hurry and come home," added Jane.

40
00:02:12.220 --> 00:02:15.837
"But you know the rules," said Huey.

41
00:02:15.838 --> 00:02:19.106
He stared at the children's blank faces.

42
00:02:19.107 --> 00:02:25.197
"The wish is granted for only one day, remember?" he reminded them.

43
00:02:25.198 --> 00:02:29.320
"Oh, yeah," they replied sadly.

44
00:02:29.321 --> 00:02:34.733
"But this is the only wish we really, really want," pleaded Bobby.

45
00:02:34.734 --> 00:02:36.975
"The other wishes were for fun.

46
00:02:36.976 --> 00:02:39.016
This is for real."

47
00:02:39.017 --> 00:02:43.689
"Yeah, this is a real wish," said Jane.

48
00:02:43.690 --> 00:02:46.092
Huey shook his head slowly.

49
00:02:46.093 --> 00:02:48.231
"I'm sorry, children.

50
00:02:48.232 --> 00:02:51.142
But rules are rules."

51
00:02:51.143 --> 00:02:54.353
Huey's fins started to glow and shine.

52
00:02:54.354 --> 00:02:57.069
The colors were more beautiful than ever.

53
00:02:57.070 --> 00:03:00.895
But the children were too sad to notice.

54
00:03:00.896 --> 00:03:05.512
"Okay, Huey. We understand," Cy said finally.

55
00:03:05.513 --> 00:03:09.690
"Then we don't have any more wishes," said Panther.

56
00:03:09.691 --> 00:03:13.655
Cy gently placed Huey back into the bucket.

57
00:03:13.656 --> 00:03:15.842
"Cheer up," said Huey.

58
00:03:15.843 --> 00:03:19.235
"I'm sure your parents will be home soon."

59
00:03:19.236 --> 00:03:22.292
With that he disappeared into his shell.

60
00:03:22.293 --> 00:03:25.327
Cy lowered him down once again.

61
00:03:25.328 --> 00:03:28.865
With heavy hearts, the children walked back home.

62
00:03:28.866 --> 00:03:33.301
They spent the rest of the day with long faces.

63
00:03:33.302 --> 00:03:36.725
"I know what will cheer us up," Panther said.

64
00:03:36.726 --> 00:03:39.856
The children were sitting on the porch eating a snack.

65
00:03:39.857 --> 00:03:42.572
"We should bake cookies for everyone."

66
00:03:42.573 --> 00:03:47.380
"What for?" asked Bobby, his mouth full of peanut butter.

67
00:03:47.381 --> 00:03:52.692
"Well, after meeting Huey, so many things happened," Panther continued.

68
00:03:52.693 --> 00:03:55.424
"Our wishes affected other people."

69
00:03:55.425 --> 00:04:02.517
"Aunt Martha, Mr. Becker and Silver," Jane counted, "and Farmer Jenkins."

70
00:04:02.518 --> 00:04:06.166
"And we made a lot of friends," said Panther.

71
00:04:06.167 --> 00:04:10.196
"That's a great idea," Cy said happily.

72
00:04:10.197 --> 00:04:12.842
So the children baked lots of cookies.

73
00:04:12.843 --> 00:04:16.728
Of course Aunt Martha and Lamb helped too.

74
00:04:16.729 --> 00:04:18.934
Outside it was getting dark.

75
00:04:18.935 --> 00:04:23.155
"We can take the cookies to everyone tomorrow," said Panther.

76
00:04:23.156 --> 00:04:26.513
Suddenly there was a knock on the door.

77
00:04:26.514 --> 00:04:29.018
"I'll get it," said Jane.

78
00:04:29.019 --> 00:04:31.419
"I wonder who it can be?"

79
00:04:31.420 --> 00:04:34.654
asked Bobby as he took another cookie from a plate.

80
00:04:34.655 --> 00:04:40.211
"Surprise!" two familiar voices shouted loudly.

81
00:04:40.212 --> 00:04:44.974
Mom and Dad had returned.

